**Facility Settings**
- The facility sidebar exposes Settings as a link to `/facility/:facilityId/settings/general`: [`facility-nav.tsx`](src/components/ui/sidebar/facility/facility-nav.tsx#L140).
- The facility route sends `/facility/:facilityId/settings*` to `SettingsLayout`: [`FacilityRoutes.tsx`](src/Routers/routes/FacilityRoutes.tsx#L46). Inside the layout, `/general` renders `GeneralSettings`, and the settings root redirects to `/settings/general`: [`layout.tsx`](src/pages/Facility/settings/layout.tsx#L76).
- Settings are route-backed subsections, not tabs inside the general details page. `GeneralSettings` renders `FacilityHome` with `appearance="settings"`: [`general.tsx`](src/pages/Facility/settings/general/general.tsx).
- Facility update permission is checked in `FacilityHome` using `usePermissions()` and the facility’s `root_org_permissions`:

```tsx
const { hasPermission } = usePermissions();

const { canUpdateFacility } = getPermissions(
  hasPermission,
  facilityData?.root_org_permissions ?? [],
);

const facilityActions = canUpdateFacility ? (
  <FacilityHomeActions
    facility={facilityData}
    isSettings={isSettings}
    buttonClassName={isSettings ? settingsButtonClassName : undefined}
    onEditCoverImage={() => setEditCoverImage(true)}
  />
) : null;
```

See [`FacilityHome.tsx`](src/components/Facility/FacilityHome.tsx#L50). This gates the edit actions; the settings route itself is not gated by this check.

**Own Profile**
- `/user/profile` matches the `/user/:tab` route, which renders `UserHome` without a username; `UserHome` then uses the logged-in user’s username. See [`UserRoutes.tsx`](src/Routers/routes/UserRoutes.tsx#L20) and [`UserHome.tsx`](src/components/Users/UserHome.tsx#L40).
- `UserHome` defines its route tabs in `TABS`; `PROFILE` uses `UserSummaryTab`, while departments and availability are facility-dependent:

```tsx
const TABS = {
  PROFILE: {
    body: UserSummaryTab,
    hidden: false,
  },
  DEPARTMENTS: {
    body: UserDepartmentsTab,
    hidden: !props.facilityId,
  },
  AVAILABILITY: {
    body: UserAvailabilityTab,
    hidden: !props.facilityId || !canViewSchedule,
  },
} satisfies Record<string, TabChildProp>;
```

See [`UserHome.tsx`](src/components/Users/UserHome.tsx#L81).

- The profile body composes sections with `UserColumns`. For example, the personal-information section uses `renderBasicInformation` as its child: [`UserSummary.tsx`](src/components/Users/UserSummary.tsx#L123). `UserColumns` is the reusable section wrapper for a heading, note, and child content: [`UserColumns.tsx`](src/components/Common/UserColumns.tsx#L9).

**Existing ABDM References**
- `careConfig.abdm.enabled` conditionally renders the patient ABHA section in [`Demography.tsx`](src/components/Patient/PatientDetailsTab/Demography.tsx#L332), enables ABHA registration for a new patient in [`PatientRegistration.tsx`](src/components/Patient/PatientRegistration.tsx#L477), and controls an encounter action’s visibility alongside clinical-read permission in [`EncounterShow.tsx`](src/pages/Encounters/EncounterShow.tsx#L204).

**ABDM Components**
Files in `src/components/Abdm`:
- [`AbhaProfileSummary.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/AbhaProfileSummary.tsx)
- [`ExternalRecordsCard.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/ExternalRecordsCard.tsx)
- [`AbhaVerificationSteps.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/AbhaVerificationSteps.tsx)
- [`ConsentRequestDialog.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/ConsentRequestDialog.tsx)
- [`FetchedRecordsDialog.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/FetchedRecordsDialog.tsx)
- [`PatientAbhaSection.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/PatientAbhaSection.tsx)
- [`AbhaVerificationDialog.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/AbhaVerificationDialog.tsx)
- [`utils.ts`](src/components/Abdm/utils.ts)
- [`AbhaRegistrationPanel.tsx`](src/components/Abdm/AbhaRegistrationPanel.tsx)

`utils.ts` exports `ABDM_USER_NOT_FOUND`, `getAbhaError(error: unknown, fallback: string): AbhaError`, `toIndianMobile`, `abhaGenderToCare`, and `getAbhaPhotoSrc`. The `getAbhaError` signature is at [`utils.ts`](src/components/Abdm/utils.ts#L7).

